  "title": "EX13 Belief Hand-Trap Discipline: Clear Red Lv.5 Blast Host Before Wingdramon Lethal",
  "description": "Seat 1 controls an unsuspended EX13-021 Wingdramon (play cost 7, 7000 DP) at 5 memory with Seat 2 at 0 security. Seat 2 just played BT2-017 WarGrowlmon (Red Lv.5) and revealed EX13-007 Guilmon + EX13-010 Growlmon in trash while keeping a large unrevealed hand. Under closed-list beliefs, Seat 2s public EX13 Red package eliminates unrelated archetypes and concentrates posterior mass on the Red Blast Ace list (EX10-010 BlackWarGreymon Ace, EX9-013 BlitzGreymon Ace, AD1-005 Gaiamon Ace, ST20-11 WarGreymon Ace), punishing a reckless direct Wingdramon attack (114) in CounterTiming. Playing BT2-096 The Ray of Victory (0) bounces the Red Lv.5 Blast host while keeping turn at 0 memory, enabling an uncounterable lethal Wingdramon swing (114).",
